	<section id="faq" class="border-t border-border bg-card/40 py-20 md:py-28">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
			<h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Questions</h2>
			<div class="mt-8 divide-y divide-border border-y border-border">
				<details class="group py-5">
					<summary
						class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink"
						>How is EasySociable different from generating carousels with Codex or ChatGPT?<svg
							xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
							width="24"
							height="24"
							viewBox="0 0 24 24"
							fill="none"
							stroke="currentColor"
							stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round"
							stroke-linejoin="round"
							class="lucide lucide-chevron-down size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition group-open:rotate-180"
							><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg
						></summary
					>
					<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
						When you use Codex or ChatGPT to generate carousel code or canvas scripts, fixing a
						single typo or a font size becomes another prompt: the agent regenerates, and the layout
						can break or other slides shift. EasySociable separates drafting from editing: your
						agent drafts the carousel, and in Studio you double-click any text to fix it yourself
						while the layout stays locked.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details class="group py-5">
					<summary
						class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink"
						>Can I switch the Brand on an already-created carousel?<svg
							xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
							width="24"
							height="24"
							viewBox="0 0 24 24"
							fill="none"
							stroke="currentColor"
							stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round"
							stroke-linejoin="round"
							class="lucide lucide-chevron-down size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition group-open:rotate-180"
							><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg
						></summary
					>
					<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
						Yes, with one click! EasySociable completely decouples content from brand styling. You
						can create brand profiles (name, handle, avatar, brand colors) and switch any existing
						carousel to another brand instantly. The colors, fonts, handles, and avatars update
						automatically across all slides—ideal for multi-account creators and marketing agencies.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details class="group py-5">
					<summary
						class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink"
						>What is the Viral Carousel Vault, and how do I clone them into my Agent?<svg
							xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
							width="24"
							height="24"
							viewBox="0 0 24 24"
							fill="none"
							stroke="currentColor"
							stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round"
							stroke-linejoin="round"
							class="lucide lucide-chevron-down size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition group-open:rotate-180"
							><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg
						></summary
					>
					<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
						We analyzed top-performing viral carousels on TikTok, Instagram, and LinkedIn and
						extracted their narrative blueprints (proven hooks, pacing, and retention structure).
						You can click &quot;Copy Prompt to Agent&quot; on any viral carousel to grab its exact
						prompt blueprint, then paste it into Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, or ChatGPT to generate
						your own post in minutes.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details class="group py-5">
					<summary
						class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink"
						>What does the copied prompt do?<svg
							xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
							width="24"
							height="24"
							viewBox="0 0 24 24"
							fill="none"
							stroke="currentColor"
							stroke-width="2"
							stroke-linecap="round"
							stroke-linejoin="round"
							class="lucide lucide-chevron-down size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition group-open:rotate-180"
							><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg
						></summary
					>
